The vendor job in .github/workflows/ci.yml checks out io-k8s-p5, rex-gpu and p5-crypt-age with full history, installs Dist::Zilla plus each sibling's authordeps, and then runs `make vendor` with the Makefile default `VENDOR ?=` (empty). The result is an empty vendor/ORDER: the artifact in run 41741299801 (main 44a9db0) is 126 bytes. The job costs about 3.5 minutes per run, and every CI run fails if a sibling's authordeps break, even though nothing from the siblings goes into the image.

The comment in ci.yml asks to "Keep the checkouts in step with the Makefile's VENDOR list". They are out of step since the siblings were released on CPAN (2026-10-21).

Done when the job follows VENDOR: no checkout and no dzil when VENDOR is empty (or the job is skipped), and the siblings in VENDOR when it is set. Lane: CI/Makefile (ocp-infra-worker or ocp-worker). Found while closing k134.

2026-11-06 (ocp-infra-worker + main agent): the CI vendor job follows the Makefile's VENDOR and holds no copy of it. Step 'list' reads it with make -s vendor-list (step output vendor); clone (make vendor-siblings) and Dist::Zilla/authordeps steps run only when that output is non-empty; make vendor and the upload always run, so the image jobs always get the artifact. New Makefile table SIBLING_HOMES (dir name -> owner/repo, 10 homes: pplu for io-k8s-p5/kubernetes-rest, Getty for the rest, owners taken from each sibling's origin URL); an unknown name fails naming the sibling. t/222: 15 subtests, 8-14 red on the old tree; 9 mutations of the new tree all red. Local dry-run of the job steps: VENDOR empty -> no clone, no tools, empty ORDER; two siblings -> cloned from the right owners, ORDER in VENDOR order; unknown name -> exit 2 with the message. YAML parses (YAML::PP, YAML::XS). Binding (image rel1106): t/222 + t/53 + t/66 Files=3 Tests=39 PASS. docs/development.md vendor section updated by the main agent. Caveat: clones are anonymous HTTPS, every vendored sibling repo must be public (as before).

